1. **Failures 1-4 (Mark all as completed / Mark items as complete)**: These are DOM-identity defects. When clicking a toggle checkbox, the app calls `render()` which rebuilds the entire `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and re-creates all `<li>` elements. This causes any previously held DOM references to become detached. The fix is to mutate the existing node in place instead of re-rendering the entire list.

2. **Failures 5, 7-10 (Editing - edit input not visible)**: The `<input class="edit">` has `display: none` because the CSS from `todomvc-app-css` hides it by default (`.todo-list li .edit { display: none }`), and the app only shows it when the `<li>` has class `editing`. But the app currently relies on the full re-render to add the `editing` class. The edit input is hidden behind `display: none` because the `editing` class is not actually being applied correctly in the real browser context.

Wait, let me re-read the code more carefully. Looking at the `render()` function:

```js
